## When to use

- Primary site navigation with grouped destinations.
- Desktop resource menus with differently sized panels.
- Navigation that needs pointer, touch and keyboard access to the same links.

## When not to use

- Application commands: use `menubar` or `dropdown-menu`.
- Persistent mobile navigation: use `sidebar` or a `sheet` composition.
- Switching local page content: use `tabs`.

## API

| Part | Props | Defaults and behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NavigationMenu` | Base UI Root props, `align` | `align="start"`; `value`/`defaultValue`, `onValueChange`, `onOpenChangeComplete`, `actionsRef`, `delay`, `closeDelay`, `orientation`, `render`, ref and native nav props pass through. Automatically appends one positioner. |
| `NavigationMenuList` | Base UI List props | List semantics and keyboard navigation. |
| `NavigationMenuItem` | Base UI Item props | Stable `value` associates trigger and content. |
| `NavigationMenuTrigger` | Base UI Trigger props | Native button, supports disabled, render, refs, callback classes/styles. Appends the owned chevron; a plain string or number child becomes the changed-run display slot. |
| `NavigationMenuContent` | Base UI Content props | Portaled content, `keepMounted=false`; caller classes/styles merge with primitive state. A direct plain string or number child becomes the owned text or quantity slot; rich children pass through unchanged. |
| `NavigationMenuLink` | Base UI Link props | Native anchor; `active`, `closeOnClick`, render, refs supported. Owns its state surface only and keeps the popup's inherited foreground. |
| `NavigationMenuIndicator` | Base UI Icon props | Static arrow within a trigger; no extra animation. |
| `NavigationMenuPositioner` | Base UI Positioner props | `side="bottom"`, `sideOffset=8`, `align="start"`, `alignOffset=0`; anchor, collision, render, refs and state callbacks pass through. |
| `navigationMenuTriggerStyle` | CVA function | Trigger classes for standalone navigation links. |

The pinned Base UI API exports Positioner, rather than Radix's Viewport export or `viewport` root prop.
Positioner contains the popup and viewport. Root already appends it; do not add a second one. Popup and
viewport have additive `data-slot` hooks. Positioner props still follow upstream composition.

## Motion contract

Authored intensity is **medium**: Navigation Menu owns one positioned surface: its popup presence, the measured shared viewport that follows the committed destination size, the entering content paint, the trigger chevron, the scoped trigger and surface palettes, and the trigger, link and content display slots, while Base UI keeps placement, hover intent, focus and unmount.

The popup enters once and the shared surface follows the destination the primitive measured; only the entering content travels, and the chevron turns on its own region.

| Phase | Properties | Token | Interruptible |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| popup enter | popup `opacity 0 → 1` with a `4px` approach from the resolved side | `popup.anchored/one-shot` · `duration.fast` | yes, a reversal continues from the current paint |
| popup exit | popup `opacity → 0`; the positioner keeps its placement | `exit.fade/one-shot` · `duration.fast` | yes (reopen mid-exit) |
| destination size revision | clamped shared shell width and height around the committed destination | `geometry.resize/measured` · `spring.sizePanel` | yes, retargets from the current size |
| content revision | entering content `opacity` and `4px` directional travel | `data.transition/directional-content` · `duration.base` | yes, the newest direction replaces the old target |
| trigger open state | chevron turns by `180deg` with no opacity or scale | `state.morph/one-shot` · `spring.snappy` | yes, retargets the current angle |
| trigger and popup paint | scoped surface, foreground, border and shadow colour; focus or an unprovable palette is immediate | `state.color/css-transition` · `duration.fast` | yes, latest committed colour |
| direct plain label | changed graphemes only, no stagger | `text.change/changed-runs` | yes, the newest diff replaces the old target |
| direct numeric content quantity | changed place values only | `number.roll/reels` | yes, retargets the current reel |

The popup's presence, the shared shell, the content paint and the chevron are four disjoint owners: the popup writes
opacity and one short transform, the shell writes width and height around the destination Base UI supplies, the
entering content writes its own opacity and travel inside the viewport, and the chevron writes its own angle. The
positioner keeps its coordinates and `--transform-origin`, so `sideOffset`/`alignOffset` and collision flips stay
native and immediate. Cadence retains no outgoing panel: an inactive `keepMounted` content stays Base UI's hidden,
inert node and receives no Cadence paint. Closed content is current on the next open without replaying hidden
updates. Portal surfaces resolve their own mode and token clock, so a nested full scope restores timing inside none;
caller custom motion must obey the same mode contract.

## Keyboard interactions

| Keys | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Tab / Shift+Tab | Enter and leave the navigation without a modal focus trap. |
| ArrowLeft / ArrowRight | Move between top-level items in horizontal orientation; logical direction follows RTL. |
| ArrowUp / ArrowDown in a vertical list | Move between top-level triggers. |
| ArrowDown / Enter / Space | Open a trigger; Tab enters its content. |
| Escape | Close and return focus to the active trigger. |
| Enter on a link | Follow the native link destination. |

## Accessibility

Root is a navigation landmark; give multiple navigation regions distinct accessible labels. Triggers
expose expanded state and content association. Base UI owns pointer hover, click/touch activation,
focus guards and outside/Escape dismissal. Disabled triggers stay focusable but cannot open a panel. Base UI owns the normal portal lifecycle; Cadence does not replace a node to reset a running transition. Cadence removes aria-hidden from Base UI 1.6’s tabbable focus sentinels within this menu; they remain empty generic spans with their original Tab redirection handlers. Keep link text meaningful and keyboard focus rings visible.

## Responsive behavior

Popup width and height are limited by Base UI's available viewport dimensions. Its viewport scrolls
when content exceeds that space. Supply responsive widths/grids for your destinations; the component
does not replace your information architecture with a mobile drawer. A passive viewport, font or
scrollbar reflow settles the shell immediately in every mode; only a committed destination measured by
the primitive is interpolated. Reduced and none never tween width or height.

## Performance

T3: one shared popup, one measured shell writer and Base UI's own post-commit measurements and
mutation/resize tracking. No timer, layout animation loop or persistent `will-change`; the chevron only
marks will-change while full motion owns its angle. Two scoped child-list observers repair newly
inserted focus sentinels; they disconnect on unmount. Geometry is limited to the popup's width and
height; nothing interpolates `top`/`left`. Inactive content unmounts by default; `keepMounted`
deliberately retains caller state and its DOM cost, without a Cadence writer. The numerical budgets
stay advisory under ADR-023 until functional migration completes.

## Notes for AI

Match the Base UI surface, including render, refs and state callback classes/styles. Do not add Radix
asChild or substitute a command menu. Keep stable item values; do not key the viewport on selection.
Use real links, label the landmark, and keep mobile content within available space.
